From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mohamed Ahmed <mohamedahmedegypt2001@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 19:49:15 +0400
Subject: drm/nouveau/dispnv50: validate modesets with IMP

Validate modesets with RM's isModePossible so configurations that exceed
display resources fail atomic_check before hardware programming. The
query includes every active head to account for shared resources,
including scanout inherited from firmware.

On GB20x, use the returned tile counts to allocate tiles and physical
windows. Preserve compatible assignments and prioritize TYPE_0 tiles for
scaling, reclaiming them from unscaled modeset heads when needed.
Transfers between heads require an early disable update to release the
old ownership before attaching the new owner.

IMP may reject modes accepted by the previous checks, so allow
imp_check=0 on hardware without tiles. The override is ignored on tiled
hardware because the reply is needed for resource allocation. Interlaced
modes are rejected even when validation is bypassed because nvdisplay
does not support them and IMP cannot describe their second field.

Signed-off-by: Mohamed Ahmed <mohamedahmedegypt2001@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 9453ca61ce56d9a17cf1295bcb67530b605f9133)
---
